    :transform
    "Params: (t: (Dataset[T]) ⇒ Dataset[U])\n\nResult: Dataset[U]\n\nConcise syntax for chaining custom transformations.\n\n1.6.0\n\nSource: https://spark.apache.org/docs/3.0.1/api/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/Dataset.html\n\nTimestamp: 2020-10-19T01:56:20.972Z",
    :stat
    "Params: \n\nResult: DataFrameStatFunctions\n\nReturns a DataFrameStatFunctions for working statistic functions support.\n\n1.6.0\n\nSource: https://spark.apache.org/docs/3.0.1/api/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/Dataset.html\n\nTimestamp: 2020-10-19T01:56:20.953Z",
    :sql-context
    "Params: \n\nResult: SQLContext\n\n\n\nSource: https://spark.apache.org/docs/3.0.1/api/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/Dataset.html\n\nTimestamp: 2020-10-19T01:56:20.952Z",
    :map-partitions
    "Params: (func: (Iterator[T]) ⇒ Iterator[U])\n\n(implicit arg0: Encoder[U])\n\nResult: Dataset[U]\n\n(Scala-specific)\nReturns a new Dataset that contains the result of applying func to each partition.\n\n\n1.6.0\n\nSource: https://spark.apache.org/docs/3.0.1/api/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/Dataset.html\n\nTimestamp: 2020-10-19T01:56:20.870Z",
    :write-to
    "Params: (table: String)\n\nResult: DataFrameWriterV2[T]\n\nCreate a write configuration builder for v2 sources.\n\nThis builder is used to configure and execute write operations. For example, to append to an\nexisting table, run:\n\nThis can also be used to create or replace existing tables:\n\n3.0.0\n\nSource: https://spark.apache.org/docs/3.0.1/api/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/Dataset.html\n\nTimestamp: 2020-10-19T01:56:20.993Z",
    :select-expr
    "Params: (exprs: String*)\n\nResult: DataFrame\n\nSelects a set of SQL expressions. This is a variant of select that accepts\nSQL expressions.\n\n2.0.0\n\nSource: https://spark.apache.org/docs/3.0.1/api/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/Dataset.html\n\nTimestamp: 2020-10-19T01:56:20.933Z",
    :limit
    "Params: (n: Int)\n\nResult: Dataset[T]\n\nReturns a new Dataset by taking the first n rows. The difference between this function\nand head is that head is an action and returns an array (by triggering query execution)\nwhile limit returns a new Dataset.\n\n\n2.0.0\n\nSource: https://spark.apache.org/docs/3.0.1/api/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/Dataset.html\n\nTimestamp: 2020-10-19T01:56:20.861Z",
    :eq
    "Params: (arg0: AnyRef)\n\nResult: Boolean\n\n\n\nSource: https://spark.apache.org/docs/3.0.1/api/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/Dataset.html\n\nTimestamp: 2020-10-19T01:56:20.794Z",
    :write-stream
    "Params: \n\nResult: DataStreamWriter[T]\n\nInterface for saving the content of the streaming Dataset out into external storage.\n\n\n2.0.0\n\nSource: https://spark.apache.org/docs/3.0.1/api/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/Dataset.html\n\nTimestamp: 2020-10-19T01:56:20.992Z",
    :encoder
    "Params: \n\nResult: Encoder[T]\n\n\n\nSource: https://spark.apache.org/docs/3.0.1/api/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/Dataset.html\n\nTimestamp: 2020-10-19T01:56:20.793Z",
    :group-by
    "Params: (cols: Column*)\n\nResult: RelationalGroupedDataset\n\nGroups the Dataset using the specified columns, so we can run aggregation on them. See\nRelationalGroupedDataset for all the available aggregate functions.\n\n2.0.0\n\nSource: https://spark.apache.org/docs/3.0.1/api/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/Dataset.html\n\nTimestamp: 2020-10-19T01:56:20.827Z",
    :to-df
    "Params: ()\n\nResult: DataFrame\n\nConverts this strongly typed collection of data to generic Dataframe. In contrast to the\nstrongly typed objects that Dataset operations work on, a Dataframe returns generic Row\nobjects that allow fields to be accessed by ordinal or name.\n\n\n1.6.0\n\nSource: https://spark.apache.org/docs/3.0.1/api/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/Dataset.html\n\nTimestamp: 2020-10-19T01:56:20.964Z",
    :observe
    "Params: (name: String, expr: Column, exprs: Column*)\n\nResult: Dataset[T]\n\nDefine (named) metrics to observe on the Dataset. This method returns an 'observed' Dataset\nthat returns the same result as the input, with the following guarantees:\n\nPlease note that continuous execution is currently not supported.\n\nThe metrics columns must either contain a literal (e.g. lit(42)), or should contain one or\nmore aggregate functions (e.g. sum(a) or sum(a + b) + avg(c) - lit(1)). Expressions that\ncontain references to the input Dataset's columns must always be wrapped in an aggregate\nfunction.\n\nA user can observe these metrics by either adding\norg.apache.spark.sql.streaming.StreamingQueryListener or a\norg.apache.spark.sql.util.QueryExecutionListener to the spark session.\n\n3.0.0\n\nSource: https://spark.apache.org/docs/3.0.1/api/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/Dataset.html\n\nTimestamp: 2020-10-19T01:56:20.881Z",
    :checkpoint
    "Params: ()\n\nResult: Dataset[T]\n\nEagerly checkpoint a Dataset and return the new Dataset. Checkpointing can be used to truncate\nthe logical plan of this Dataset, which is especially useful in iterative algorithms where the\nplan may grow exponentially. It will be saved to files inside the checkpoint\ndirectory set with SparkContext#setCheckpointDir.\n\n\n2.1.0\n\nSource: https://spark.apache.org/docs/3.0.1/api/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/Dataset.html\n\nTimestamp: 2020-10-19T01:56:20.752Z",
    :##
    "Params: ()\n\nResult: Int\n\n\n\nSource: https://spark.apache.org/docs/3.0.1/api/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/Dataset.html\n\nTimestamp: 2020-10-19T01:56:20.731Z",
    :to-string
    "Params: ()\n\nResult: String\n\n\n\nSource: https://spark.apache.org/docs/3.0.1/api/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/Dataset.html\n\nTimestamp: 2020-10-19T01:56:20.969Z",
    :union-by-name
    "Params: (other: Dataset[T])\n\nResult: Dataset[T]\n\nReturns a new Dataset containing union of rows in this Dataset and another Dataset.\n\nThis is different from both UNION ALL and UNION DISTINCT in SQL. To do a SQL-style set\nunion (that does deduplication of elements), use this function followed by a distinct.\n\nThe difference between this function and union is that this function\nresolves columns by name (not by position):\n\n2.3.0\n\nSource: https://spark.apache.org/docs/3.0.1/api/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/Dataset.html\n\nTimestamp: 2020-10-19T01:56:20.978Z",
    :spark-session
    "Params: \n\nResult: SparkSession\n\n\n\nSource: https://spark.apache.org/docs/3.0.1/api/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/Dataset.html\n\nTimestamp: 2020-10-19T01:56:20.951Z",
    :create-temp-view
    "Params: (viewName: String)\n\nResult: Unit\n\nCreates a local temporary view using the given name. The lifetime of this\ntemporary view is tied to the SparkSession that was used to create this Dataset.\n\nLocal temporary view is session-scoped. Its lifetime is the lifetime of the session that\ncreated it, i.e. it will be automatically dropped when the session terminates. It's not\ntied to any databases, i.e. we can't use db1.view1 to reference a local temporary view.\n\n\n2.0.0\n\nAnalysisException if the view name is invalid or already exists\n\nSource: https://spark.apache.org/docs/3.0.1/api/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/Dataset.html\n\nTimestamp: 2020-10-19T01:56:20.769Z",
    :columns
    "Params: \n\nResult: Array[String]\n\nReturns all column names as an array.\n\n\n1.6.0\n\nSource: https://spark.apache.org/docs/3.0.1/api/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/Dataset.html\n\nTimestamp: 2020-10-19T01:56:20.762Z",
    :as
    "Params: (implicit arg0: Encoder[U])\n\nResult: Dataset[U]\n\nReturns a new Dataset where each record has been mapped on to the specified type. The\nmethod used to map columns depend on the type of U:\n\nIf the schema of the Dataset does not match the desired U type, you can use select\nalong with alias or as to rearrange or rename as required.\n\nNote that as[] only changes the view of the data that is passed into typed operations,\nsuch as map(), and does not eagerly project away any columns that are not present in\nthe specified class.\n\n\n1.6.0\n\nSource: https://spark.apache.org/docs/3.0.1/api/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/Dataset.html\n\nTimestamp: 2020-10-19T01:56:20.747Z",
    :drop-duplicates
    "Params: ()\n\nResult: Dataset[T]\n\nReturns a new Dataset that contains only the unique rows from this Dataset.\nThis is an alias for distinct.\n\nFor a static batch Dataset, it just drops duplicate rows. For a streaming Dataset, it\nwill keep all data across triggers as intermediate state to drop duplicates rows. You can use\nwithWatermark to limit how late the duplicate data can be and system will accordingly limit\nthe state. In addition, too late data older than watermark will be dropped to avoid any\npossibility of duplicates.\n\n\n2.0.0\n\nSource: https://spark.apache.org/docs/3.0.1/api/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/Dataset.html\n\nTimestamp: 2020-10-19T01:56:20.791Z",
    :to-json
    "Params: \n\nResult: Dataset[String]\n\nReturns the content of the Dataset as a Dataset of JSON strings.\n\n2.0.0\n\nSource: https://spark.apache.org/docs/3.0.1/api/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/Dataset.html\n\nTimestamp: 2020-10-19T01:56:20.965Z",
    :drop
    "Params: (colName: String)\n\nResult: DataFrame\n\nReturns a new Dataset with a column dropped. This is a no-op if schema doesn't contain\ncolumn name.\n\nThis method can only be used to drop top level columns. the colName string is treated\nliterally without further interpretation.\n\n\n2.0.0\n\nSource: https://spark.apache.org/docs/3.0.1/api/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/Dataset.html\n\nTimestamp: 2020-10-19T01:56:20.785Z",
    :rollup
    "Params: (cols: Column*)\n\nResult: RelationalGroupedDataset\n\nCreate a multi-dimensional rollup for the current Dataset using the specified columns,\nso we can run aggregation on them.\nSee RelationalGroupedDataset for all the available aggregate functions.\n\n2.0.0\n\nSource: https://spark.apache.org/docs/3.0.1/api/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/Dataset.html\n\nTimestamp: 2020-10-19T01:56:20.907Z",
    :notify-all
    "Params: ()\n\nResult: Unit\n\n\n\nSource: https://spark.apache.org/docs/3.0.1/api/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/Dataset.html\n\nTimestamp: 2020-10-19T01:56:20.878Z",
    :create-or-replace-temp-view
    "Params: (viewName: String)\n\nResult: Unit\n\nCreates a local temporary view using the given name. The lifetime of this\ntemporary view is tied to the SparkSession that was used to create this Dataset.\n\n\n2.0.0\n\nSource: https://spark.apache.org/docs/3.0.1/api/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/Dataset.html\n\nTimestamp: 2020-10-19T01:56:20.767Z",
    :persist
    "Params: ()\n\nResult: Dataset.this.type\n\nPersist this Dataset with the default storage level (MEMORY_AND_DISK).\n\n\n1.6.0\n\nSource: https://spark.apache.org/docs/3.0.1/api/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/Dataset.html\n\nTimestamp: 2020-10-19T01:56:20.886Z",
    :create-or-replace-global-temp-view
    "Params: (viewName: String)\n\nResult: Unit\n\nCreates or replaces a global temporary view using the given name. The lifetime of this\ntemporary view is tied to this Spark application.\n\nGlobal temporary view is cross-session. Its lifetime is the lifetime of the Spark application,\ni.e. it will be automatically dropped when the application terminates. It's tied to a system\npreserved database global_temp, and we must use the qualified name to refer a global temp\nview, e.g. SELECT * FROM global_temp.view1.\n\n\n2.2.0\n\nSource: https://spark.apache.org/docs/3.0.1/api/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/Dataset.html\n\nTimestamp: 2020-10-19T01:56:20.766Z",
    :coalesce
    "Params: (numPartitions: Int)\n\nResult: Dataset[T]\n\nReturns a new Dataset that has exactly numPartitions partitions, when the fewer partitions\nare requested. If a larger number of partitions is requested, it will stay at the current\nnumber of partitions. Similar to coalesce defined on an RDD, this operation results in\na narrow dependency, e.g. if you go from 1000 partitions to 100 partitions, there will not\nbe a shuffle, instead each of the 100 new partitions will claim 10 of the current partitions.\n\nHowever, if you're doing a drastic coalesce, e.g. to numPartitions = 1,\nthis may result in your computation taking place on fewer nodes than\nyou like (e.g. one node in the case of numPartitions = 1). To avoid this,\nyou can call repartition. This will add a shuffle step, but means the\ncurrent upstream partitions will be executed in parallel (per whatever\nthe current partitioning is).\n\n\n1.6.0\n\nSource: https://spark.apache.org/docs/3.0.1/api/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/Dataset.html\n\nTimestamp: 2020-10-19T01:56:20.755Z",
    :random-split-as-list
    "Params: (weights: Array[Double], seed: Long)\n\nResult: List[Dataset[T]]\n\nReturns a Java list that contains randomly split Dataset with the provided weights.\n\n\nweights for splits, will be normalized if they don't sum to 1.\n\nSeed for sampling.\n\n2.0.0\n\nSource: https://spark.apache.org/docs/3.0.1/api/scala/org/apache/spark/sql/Dataset.html\n\nTimestamp: 2020-10-19T01:56:20.893Z",
    :equals
